  "observations": [
    "All three expression types use two independent original-pose sources, with separate anatomical left/right patch selection. The near/far brow widths remain those of the original perspective.",
    "innerUp changes the actual medial slope and down lowers the medial section. Revised outerUp sources now raise formerly weak exposed outer segments by about3–5 native pixels; actual amplitude is softer than the initial prompt and differs across the four brows.",
    "Clip lower edges leave space above the original upper-lid creases. Coarse central/outer bang interiors are protected separately; thin eyebrow-crossing strands and the stylized original brow-through-hair marks require visual continuity inspection.",
    "Final source eyebrows retain the existing desaturated gray-violet treatment. No mirrored or scaled brow image is proposed.",
    "Protection polygons are independent comparison regions in original source coordinates. They cover real eyelids/white/iris and coarse bangs, rather than the oversized old eye patch rectangles that also contain forehead skin.",
    "Use the exact approved eye/mouth/gaze combination as the diagnostic baseline. Must check open, half and closed eyes because drawing brows after eye patches should not restore the original open eyelids.",
    "Source preparation can change fine hair pixels inside the brow strip. Pixel checks of coarse protected hair do not replace close-up visual review of those thin crossing strands.",
    "Only one independent drawing exists per action per pose. These bounds do not imply continuous eyebrow strength drawings or approval of new eyebrow expressions."
  ],
